  "reason": "The records collectively make the later result plausibly reconstructible. R9 supplies the exact 1000 °C SPS treatment for mechanically milled CoCrFeNiTi, a compositionally close HEA, while R2, R5, R14, R17, and R19 show that SPS of mechanically alloyed HEA powders produces dense bodies, precipitation, oxide dispersions, and high hardness. Most importantly, R7 connects increasing SPS temperature, uniformly distributed oxides, enhanced diffusion, and improved passivation, while R1, R4, R11, and R16 establish that dense oxide/passive films suppress oxygen diffusion and ionic penetration and improve oxidation and corrosion resistance. An expert could therefore combine temperature-optimized SPS with oxide-assisted densification and passivation, although the exact MgAlTiVFeCo oxide identities and numerical optimum would still require experiment."
